- **NEP (₹1,117.77 cr)** was read directly off the Revenue Account's "Premium earned (Net)" line — this is NEP, not NWP; the gross-to-net premium schedule needed to isolate NWP was not legible and is left blank.
- <span style="color:#1E3A8A;font-weight:600">Claims ratio (64.66%)</span> and <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">Combined ratio (115.9%)</span> are sourced from secondary aggregator/news sources (PolicyX citing IRDAI data; Economic Times citing rating-agency/company disclosures) because the primary Analytical Ratios table in the Annual Report had its numeric values garbled by OCR — flagged as a fallback rather than the preferred primary-document figure.
- <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">PAT:</span> Independent news confirms ManipalCigna posted a **net loss in FY23** (unlike peers Star Health, Care, and Niva Bupa, which were profitable that year), per Cafemutual's reporting on standalone health insurers' FY23 results — but the exact rupee loss figure could not be confirmed from the source documents and is therefore left blank rather than estimated.
- **Net worth, AUM, Investment yield, Retail health GWP, FY23-specific retail health market share, Expense/EoM/Commission ratio breakdowns, and IFRS-basis PAT/claims ratio** are not disclosed or legibly extractable in any of the sources reviewed for this period and are left blank per the no-estimate rule.

If a cleaner, text-native (non-scanned) version of the FY23 Annual Report or the Q4FY23 IRDAI NL disclosure becomes available, the blank cells above (particularly NWP, Net worth, EoM/Commission/Expense ratios, and exact PAT) could likely be filled with primary-source figures.</ans>
